    F-6 Harm A: the Collaborator's own code as an un-rewritable rulebook (cheap cross-platform pass) (#33)
    
    run_command has no filesystem fence (write_file/read_file do), so a governed shell could overwrite
    the Collaborator's own governance code and neuter F1 ("the model can never self-originate an
    autonomous emission"). This closes the AUTONOMOUS self-rewrite path cross-platform, WITHOUT
    hard-fencing run_command (which would kill the system maintenance the Collaborator is for):
    
    - collaborator/codefence.py (new): PROTECTED_ROOTS (collaborator/ + salienceos/), disjoint_from_code()
      workspace guard, names_code_root() (porous DiD recognizer), code_protection_available() (False for
      now — OS-level prevention is a deferred follow-up).
    - Session construction refuses a workspace overlapping the code root (both directions).
    - governance seam: a PROPOSER run_command naming the code root is hard-denied; run_command AUTONOMY
      is withheld (act_then_report floored to propose_first) until code protection is verified, so an
      unfenced shell can never AUTO-run — it always gets a human hand; honest code_protected flag +
      names_code_root surfaced in the HELD preview; audit-only code-touch tag.
    - approve() re-asserts the code-root deny for a collaborator-origin held run_command (moment-of-use).
    - tools.py docstring made honest (no longer claims run_command containment).
    
    Deliberate behavior diff: an act_then_report run_command is now HELD, not auto-run (two tests updated
    to route through approve()). OS-level structural prevention of a human-APPROVED rewrite (a read-only
    bind of the code root / a separate maintenance trust domain) is the deferred follow-up, converging
    with PR B and the third-agent arc.
    
    Internal red-team pass (reproduce-before-accept): all 6 guarantees held, no finding survived.
    Suite: 536 tests, 3 skipped, green (python -m unittest discover -s tests).
    
    
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Rpuvh681reoP8Xf53NfcGU
    
